      "title": "Duke Ellington: Band Colour and Composition",
      "level": 1,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "**Track:** history | **Difficulty:** 5/10 | **Time:** ~10 min"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "overview",
      "title": "Overview",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Edward Kennedy 'Duke' Ellington (1899–1974) led one of history's greatest big bands, composing thousands of works treating each section as a colour palette."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "masterworks",
      "title": "Masterworks",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "*Mood Indigo*, *Take the A Train*, *Black, Brown and Beige*, *Such Sweet Thunder*. Wrote for specific players — Ben Webster, Johnny Hodges, Cootie Williams."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "orchestration",
      "title": "Orchestration",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Same chord, different voicing = different room. Céilí bands borrow sectional thinking for accordion vs fiddle vs brass countermelodies."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "arranging",
      "title": "Arranging",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Vary texture each turn. Solo space over rich backgrounds. Shout chorus for climax — transferable to festival sets."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
